From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel <daniel@matv.io>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] swstats_cpu: normalise channel sums to the 8-bit domain

UNITS-MISMATCH BUG (upstream candidate, affects every >8bpp sensor on
the soft ISP): SWSTATS_ACCUMULATE_LINE_STATS accumulated sum_ in RAW
bit-depth units -- the div parameter (1 for 8-bit/10P variants, 4 for
10-bit, 16 for 12-bit) only scaled the yHistogram index, never the
channel sums. The sole consumer of sum_, the simple IPA's AWB
(src/ipa/simple/algorithms/awb.cpp), subtracts
offset = blackLevel * nPixels with blackLevel in 8-BIT units
(context.activeState.blc.level, yaml value >> 8). On a 10-bit sensor
(fajita: IMX376/IMX371, pedestal ~64 raw = 16 in 8-bit) only ~1/4 of
the black pedestal was removed from the sums, so 3/4 of it polluted
the grey-world ratios. Near black the residual pedestal dominates the
signal, the per-channel gain errors of a few percent land right at the
gamma-table toe, and the toe amplifies them into the violet cast on
night shots.

Fix: divide each sample by div at accumulation time so sum_ is in the
8-bit domain for every input bit depth, making the AWB's 8-bit offset
correct as-is. Per-sample integer truncation (<1 LSB) is negligible
for AWB averages. The div=1 variants are unchanged (x/1 folds away).
The yHistogram was already normalised, so AGC/BLC are unaffected. The
AF-series sharpness metric (patches 05-08) normalises by sumG, so its
absolute scale grows 4x on 10-bit sensors -- harmless, AF only ever
compares sharpness ratiometrically against its own running peak.

Companion: patch 11 (AWB illuminant-range clamp). With the pedestal
correctly removed, near-black sums become small and the gain ratios
noisy; the clamp keeps them inside physically plausible bounds.
---
 include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swisp_stats.h | 4 ++++
 src/libcamera/software_isp/swstats_cpu.cpp            | 6 +++---
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swisp_stats.h
+++ b/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/swisp_stats.h
@@ -29,6 +29,10 @@
 	bool valid;
 	/**
 	 * \brief Sums of colour channels of all the sampled pixels
+	 *
+	 * The sums are normalised to the 8-bit range regardless of the
+	 * input bit depth, matching the units of the black level that the
+	 * statistics consumers subtract from them.
 	 */
 	RGB<uint64_t> sum_;
 	/**
--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/swstats_cpu.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/swstats_cpu.cpp
@@ -178,9 +178,9 @@
 	uint64_t sharpness = 0;
 
 #define SWSTATS_ACCUMULATE_LINE_STATS(div) \
-	sumR += r;                         \
-	sumG += g;                         \
-	sumB += b;                         \
+	sumR += r / (div);                 \
+	sumG += g / (div);                 \
+	sumB += b / (div);                 \
                                            \
 	yVal = r * kRedYMul;               \
 	yVal += g * kGreenYMul;            \
